  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1210 PM CST Sun Nov 15 2026\n\nUpper-level troughing in the east continues to drift eastward\naway from the Quad State. Strong ridging moves over and broadens\nearly week. Dry conditions continue today through much of the\nweek ahead with early morning fog possible in climatologically\nfavored locations (mainly near rivers/lakes). Dew points \ncontinue to be significantly lowered away from the NBM which is \nsharply overestimating surface moisture levels in this dry \npattern. Today and tomorrow will see highs in the upper half of \nthe 50s, with lows just below freezing. An embedded upper low \ndrifts from the Southern Plains to the Deep South Sunday night \ninto Monday.\n\nA large surface high continues to keep conditions dry through\nthe workweek. Increasingly southerly flow will allow a gradual \nwarming trend, with near normal temperatures midweek, and above \nnormal temperatures for the end of the week. A shortwave \ndeveloping in the lee of the Rockies Wednesday quickly moves \nnortheastward to the Dakotas with the surface front nowhere near\nthe Quad State. A second shortwave Friday-Saturday has a track \nslightly further east which might bring the tail of a cold front\nthrough over the weekend, or just fizzle out again with the \nmain system too far north.",
